FINDING (does not fail a written criterion; flagged for the lead)
--------------------------------------------------------------------
The committed test file contains no test that would fail if change #1 (the
category check) were reverted. Mutation-tested, not guessed: in the HEAD
worktree I applied ONLY the pattern change ("usaa transfer" inserted, the
`catLower == "transfer"` clause left absent -- verified by grep showing
line 156 as `if catLower == "credit card payment" {`) and ran
`go test ./internal/services/classifier/... -run TestIsInternalTransfer`:
    ok  	budget2/internal/services/classifier	0.002s   (exit 0)
The whole suite passes with the category feature removed. Cause: the spec's
own required row #1 uses Description "USAA Transfer", which also matches the
newly added "usaa transfer" pattern, so it is satisfied via the pattern path
and never reaches the category branch. The category feature is therefore
correct (proved by my C1 probe) but unguarded against future regression.
Strictly against the written criteria this is a PASS -- the criteria require
the five listed rows to be present and passing and red->green to be shown, and
both are demonstrated -- but a one-line addition such as
    {"transfer category isolated", "WALMART GROCERY", "Transfer", -100, true}
would close it. Offered as a finding, not a repair; I did not edit any file.
